{
  "$comment": [
    "Room scoring parity table (ARCHITECTURE §4.13, PRD §4.5): every row of PRD §4.5.5 (Classic, T = 20 s), the grace boundaries at 400 and 600 ms (AC-ROM-08), voids, rounding, the ranking and the gap to the player above.",
    "Replayed by Vitest against src/engine/scoring/room.ts, and from SQL-14 by generated tests against the room answer and reveal RPCs.",
    "points: one answer. limitMs is the player's T with any +50% extension (null when the timer is off, which always scores as Accuracy). tServerMs runs from the server issuing the options to receiving the answer, tClientMs from the phone rendering them to the press. The effective time is clamp(max(tServer - 400, tClient), 0, T); an answer received after the player's deadline (tServerMs above limitMs) is inside the grace and earns no speed bonus. Speed is round(300 × (1 - t / T)), half up. streakBefore counts consecutive correct answers before this question; expect gives the points, the streak after it and the effective time kept for the ranking's tie-break (null unless correct).",
    "windows: an answer received offsetMs after the deadline (deadline null: the timer is off): in_time, grace (accepted, no speed bonus) up to 500 ms after, then late (rejected).",
    "sequences: a run of answers through one game, so streaks carry across questions and a voided question leaves them untouched.",
    "ranking: score, higher first; then the lower sum of effective times over correct answers; equal on both share the rank (the next rank skips). gaps: the nearest seat ranked ahead and the points between; for the leader, the lead over the next seat."
  ],
